From 1381aa30b6a63479673c1f2eebfed97ae5b6a5cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <virajslko@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:52:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/17] render: never render a project whose renderer failed to
 build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Project::render builds the renderer lazily on its first call: it creates the
RenderContext, then CWallpaper::fromWallpaper. When that throws (a missing
WE asset, an object with a missing parent, …) wp_render_frame catches the
exception at the API boundary, but renderContext is already set and
wallpaper is still null. The next wp_render_frame skips the build (the
context exists) and dereferences the null wallpaper: SIGSEGV.

Return early when there is no wallpaper. The project keeps reporting 1x1,
which a host can read as "broken"; it can be destroyed normally.

Reproduced by patches/lwe/tests/host_api_test.cpp
render_after_failed_build_returns (livepaper repo): a scene whose only object
names a parent that does not exist loads, fails its build, and the second
render crashed.

Origin: ours
Why: a scene that fails its renderer build (missing assets) must not crash the host on the next frame (docs/player/spikes/lwe-core.md §4.4)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.cpp
index 26a9ace..7fc8ec0 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Project.cpp
@@ -227,6 +227,12 @@ void WallpaperEngine::Project::render () {
 	this->renderContext->albumArtUrlChange (this->mediaInfo.url);
     }
 
+    // the renderer failed to build on an earlier call (CWallpaper::fromWallpaper threw after the
+    // render context was created): there is nothing to render, ever — and wallpaper is null
+    if (this->wallpaper == nullptr) {
+	return;
+    }
+
     this->wallpaper->render ();
 }
 
